            <ArticleTitle>A complication of subarachnoid phenol blockade.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>260-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors have described a fatal complication which occurred after a cervical subarachnoid block with phenol in glycerine. As a result of this experience they advocate the use of a dose of phenol of not more than 2 ml, which is smaller than that sometimes recommended, and also emphasise most strongly the importance of careful positioning of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
